RF.put("questb:b74",{"8634":{"id":8634,"t":"Enigma Boots","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,950, 0.66 times as much.","obj":"Bring the Qiraji Bindings of Dominance, 2 Idols of the Sun, 5 Silver Scarabs and 5 Crystal Scarabs to Kandrostrasz in Ahn'Qiraj. This quest also requires Neutral faction with the Brood of Nozdormu.\nQiraji Bindings of Dominance Viscidus in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Princess Huhuran in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of the Sun Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Silver Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Crystal Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 0 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"Qiraji magic is strong and ancient. The most powerful qiraji wield items of such might, they'd give pause even to a dragon.\nBring me the qiraji bindings of dominance and other minor components by and I'll create a set of powerful boots for you.\nYou will find them useful in the fight against the enemy.","rew":"You will receive:\nEnigma Boots\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"You've acquired the items I requested, ‹name›?","done":"You've done well, ‹name›. You've proven you're no ordinary mortal.\nI give you these with the confidence they'll aid you in crushing the vile qiraji.\nStart Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Mage Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8634\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 13,200 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Enigma Boots this quest\nBring the Qiraji Bindings of Dominance, 2 Idols of the Sun, 5 Silver Scarabs and 5 Crystal Scarabs to Kandrostrasz in Ahn'Qiraj.\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8794":{"id":8794,"t":"The Horde Needs Your Help!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 10. Gives 650 experience instead of 9,500, 0.07 times as much.","obj":"Speak with Warlord Gorchuk in Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits.","desc":"Hello, I'm glad that you've decided to hear me out. The Horde needs all of the help that it can get to prepare for the Ahn'Qiraj War, and that means that we need you! Even now as we speak, official collectors are gathering the necessary material needed for the upcoming war, but we won't be able to meet our goals without your assistance, ‹name›!\nYou should go speak with the guy in charge, Warlord Gorchuk. What do you say, ‹class›? Will you help out with the vital preparations?","rew":"Experience: 650","done":"Throm'ka, ‹class›! Good to see so many of the Horde, such as yourself, ‹name›, coming out to lend your support in laying the groundwork for the upcoming Ahn'Qiraj War. The effort here will ensure that we are victorious against the Silithid and their evil masters hidden away inside Ahn'Qiraj.\nSo now that you are here, be sure to speak with the various collectors and offer your assistance in gathering those materials that you are suited to.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":51.6,"y":66.4,"n":"Senior Sergeant Kai'jin","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":29.8,"y":67.3,"n":"Warlord Gorchuk","e":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"554":{"id":554,"t":"Stormpike's Deciphering","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Ensorcelled Parchment to Prospector Stormpike in Ironforge.\nEnsorcelled Parchment Worn Wooden Chest\nProvided: Ensorcelled Parchment","desc":"Prospector Stormpike is a master of decryption and deciphering. If you take the parchment you found to him, then with luck he can make sense of it. Stormpike is currently studying in the Prospector headquarters in Ironforge.\nAnd when you see him tell him you spoke with me - I've been sending him quite a lot of business lately.","rew":"Money: 50 0 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,550\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"More interruptions?\nAh, this parchment is covered with a very intricate, finely woven spell. I can untangle it, of course, but it's going to take time. And time is very valuable to me...\nPerhaps I will just purchase it from you?","done":"A wise decision. I don't believe there is a scholar other than myself with the skills to translate this scroll. And if its contents prove interesting, fear not. I will send for you.\nHillsbrad Foothills Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":50.6,"y":57.1,"n":"Loremaster Dibbs","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.1,"y":23,"n":"Prospector Stormpike","e":1}],"cats":["alterac-mountains"]},"8154":{"id":8154,"t":"Arathi Basin Resources!","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 3,900 experience instead of 5,500, 0.71 times as much.","obj":"Win the battle for Arathi Basin, get an Arathi Resource Crate, and return it to Sergeant Maclear at Refuge Pointe.\nArathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"War must be fought with soldiers, any soldier will tell you. They'll also say that a battle fought with poor gear or on an empty stomach is lost before it starts!\nThat is why Arathi Basin is important. There are key areas in the basin that hold essential resources. Metals, weapons, food, lumber - all are needed, and all can be gained there.\nThat is what I want from you, ‹name›. Enter Arathi Basin, win the battle by holding more bases than the enemy, and return to me with a crate of resources.","rew":"Money: 1 95 1 gold, 95 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,900\n+200 reputation with The League of Arathor","back":"Do you have the resource crate, ‹name›? The League of Arathor can't fight a decent battle without them...","done":"You got the resources! Great job! I'll send the resources to our quartermasters, who can quickly disperse them to our troops.\nThank you, ‹name›. Indeed, performing successful missions like the one you achieved are how wars are truly won.\nLevel 45 , requires level 40 Difficulty 40 41 43 48 57 Side Alliance Type PvP Shareable No Quest ID 8154","cats":["arathi-basin"]},"8394":{"id":8394,"t":"Claiming Arathi Basin","lv":49,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Arathi Basin Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"Winning a war is about more than just outsmarting and outfighting your opponent. Victory often comes down to simply producing more than your enemy.\nWhat we have in Arathi Basin is a sizeable supply of resources for whichever side manages to claim it first.\nIf the Alliance comes out victorious, it'll mean more swords and pikes for our troops. If the Horde were to win, those swords and pikes would still get made, they'd just be pointed at us! Now is the time to help the Alliance in Arathi Basin, ‹name›.","rew":"Money: 70 0 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,550\n+100 reputation with The League of Arathor","back":"Tell me, what are the news from the front?","done":"Good work, soldier! Keep it up and we'll have the Horde running all the way back to Orgrimmar.\nDun Morogh Darnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":35.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58,"y":34.2,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":81.2,"y":38.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"1034":{"id":1034,"t":"The Ruins of Stardust","lv":23,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 5 Handfuls of Stardust to Pelturas in Astranaar.\n5 Handful of Stardust Stardust Covered Bush","desc":"Elune's Tear washed clear some of my daughter's sickness. Her nightmares are lessened and I thank the goddess for her blessing. But ... fever still rages within her.\nOrendil told me of a frosted dust found among the Ruins of Stardust. Perhaps it will abate Relara's fever. Gather some of the dust, then please return to me.\nThe Ruins of Stardust lie to the south, ‹name›. May Elune speed your journey.","rew":"Money: 15 0 gold, 15 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,850\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Do you yet have the Stardust, ‹name›?","done":"You gathered the dust! I will create a poultice from these -- it should bring down Relara's fever.\nThank you again, ‹name›. Without your help, my child would surely perish.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":37.4,"y":51.8,"n":"Pelturas Whitemoon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"714":{"id":714,"t":"Gyro... What?","lv":37,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Gyrochronatom to Lotwil Veriatus in the Badlands.\nGyrochronatom Advanced Target Dummy 60 % , Venture Co. Mechanic 0.4 % , Venture Co. Shredder 0.4 % , Venture Co. Tinkerer 0.2 % and 1 more","desc":"‹name›, you've done your job well beyond all standards.\n<Lotwil's obviously distracted by his work.>\nIf we ever meet in Kharanos, feel free to come apply for work.\nWhoops! Quick, grab the... yes, that. Thanks.\nNow I just need one more thing. It's a small part, but rather crucial, I'm afraid: a gyrochronatom.\nIf you could just go grab one and bring it to me, I should be ready to complete this.","rew":"Experience: 2,850","back":"Yes, yes, yes. Just a moment.","done":"HA!\n<Lotwil grabs the gyrochronatom from you.>\nPerfect... just about done. No, really. I AM almost done now. This project is my top priority... at the moment. Let me pop this into place, and you can see for yourself what you've helped me create. It'll just take me a few more minutes... maybe... possibly longer. Well, maybe a lot longer. We'll see...","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":25.9,"y":44.9,"n":"Lotwil Veriatus","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"96634":{"id":96634,"t":"Camping 101 cooking","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Zarrin in Dolanaar to learn to become a cook.\nLearn cooking from Zarrin in Dolanaar","desc":"So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, ‹class›. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp.","back":"A good campfire is the foundation to any good camp.","done":"With this, you'll be able to set up a camp anywhere out in the wilderness. What you've learned is just the basics, so you won't be able to place too many furnishings around it.\nRaise your cooking skill and you might just be able to learn to make even bigger fires.\nYou can also learn the basics of furnishing your campsites from other tradeskill trainers if you're savvy in their skills.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":57.6,"y":56.6,"n":"Lyreena Duskblade","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":57,"y":61.2,"n":"Zarrin","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94314":{"id":94314,"t":"Craftsmans writ cindercloth robe","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Cindercloth Robe\nCindercloth Robe","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Cindercloth Robe, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Cindercloth Robe Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94314","cats":["crafting"]},"94234":{"id":94234,"t":"Craftsmans writ shadow goggles","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Shadow Goggles\nShadow Goggles","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Shadow Goggles, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"Hey! Watch where you're walking!","done":"My new shadow goggles!\n<Without another word, the goblin tossed a handful of coins your way with one hand while the other swiped the item out of your grasp. The transaction was completed and his attention lost before you had a moment to process what happened.>","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":59,"y":62.6,"n":"Ziz Fizziks","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"954":{"id":954,"t":"Bashal'Aran","lv":12,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the source of the strange blue aura in the ruins of Bashal'Aran.\nFind the place the quest sends you to.","desc":"The ruins of Bashal'Aran to the east are overrun with demonic minions. The sprites and satyrs that have taken up residence in the area feed upon the magical energies of the area, their powers growing from continued exposure.\nEven with that, I have noticed that there is one shrine they will not approach. On the western side of the ruins, atop a small bluff, a strange blue aura permeates... There must be an explanation to the demons' reluctance.\nI would like you to investigate it.","rew":"Experience: 675\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Ahh... To what could I possibly owe the exceedingly special honor of a ‹race› such as yourself as company. Truly it says much of my current companions--with no offense to my hosts, the noble grells and satyrs--that your presence could be considered an improvement.\nBut please, do not let my uncivil tongue drive you from the place. It has indeed been many years, decades even, since I had civil accompaniment.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":37.4,"y":40.1,"n":"Thundris Windweaver","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":44.2,"y":36.3,"n":"Asterion","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"98394":{"id":98394,"t":"The great cat spirit","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Seek out the Great Cat Spirit in southern part Moonglade and learn what it has to share with you about the nature of the cat.","desc":"In the southern part of Moonglade, on a hill overlooking the bridge, resides a wise and cunning being we call the Great Cat Spirit.\nMuch like the Great Bear Spirit, this spirit has served as a tutor and mentor to druids that desire to take the feline shape. All druids eventually seek its wisdom, and if you desire to take the form of a cat, you will as well.\nGo meet with the Great Cat Spirit and learn what it will teach you.","done":"I see you have come to learn to draw upon my spirit. Good. Let us see if you are ready to take my shape.","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.4,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","s":1},{"z":"Moonglade","x":54.6,"y":75,"n":"Great Cat Spirit","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"7674":{"id":7674,"t":"Black Ram Exchange","lv":1,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Black Ram","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSwift Brown Ram Swift Gray Ram Swift White Ram","back":"[PH] Ye bring me yer old ram, I will trade it in for one from the new pack! The new ram will be just as fast as yer old one, but with a new look to him. You can look at the swift rams here to see what ye will have to choose from.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.5,"y":50.6,"n":"Veron Amberstill","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"234":{"id":234,"t":"Coldridge Valley Mail Delivery","lv":4,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 0 instead of 7c. New rewards: Mining for Dummies, Wild Harvest, Pelt Collecting for Beginners.","obj":"Deliver the letter to Grelin Whitebeard.\nA Letter to Grelin Whitebeard\nProvided: A Letter to Grelin Whitebeard","desc":"If I remember correctly, Grelin's camp is down the road to the southeast. No doubt he'll be eager to get his mail.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMining for Dummies Wild Harvest Pelt Collecting for Beginners\nNew in Forever: Mining for Dummies, Wild Harvest, Pelt Collecting for Beginners.\nExperience: 270\n+75 reputation with Ironforge\n+75 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Is there something I can help you with?","done":"Ahh, excellent. It's been a while since I received word from Ironforge.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":22.6,"y":71.4,"n":"Talin Keeneye","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":25.1,"y":75.7,"n":"Grelin Whitebeard","e":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"314":{"id":314,"t":"Protecting the Herd","lv":12,"min":6,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Rudra Amberstill wants you to slay Vagash and bring his fang to her at the Ram ranch.\nFang of Vagash Vagash","desc":"We heard the cries in the middle of the night. Then this morning, sure enough, the herd was missing two rams. That dastardly beast known as Vagash has been preying on our livelihood. With most of King Magni's army off in distant lands fighting with the Alliance, there is no one to keep Vagash at bay.\nPerhaps you are brave enough to seek out the beast and slay him. Bring me one of his fangs and I will reward you. Vagash lurks just above the ranch here, but be warned, he is deadly.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nRancher's Trousers Soft Leather Tunic Coldridge Hammer\nExperience: 900\n+100 reputation with Ironforge\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Vagash still terrorizes the herd! Please help us by killing the wretched beast.","done":"Very well done! Veron will be so happy when he hears the good news. To kill Vagash is no easy task. I imagine one day you'll be fighting alongside King Magni's men on the Alliance Front.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.1,"y":49.8,"n":"Rudra Amberstill","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"6394":{"id":6394,"t":"Thazz'ril's Pick","lv":4,"min":3,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Thazz'ril's Pick to Foreman Thazz'ril.\nThazz'ril's Pick Thazz'ril's Pick","desc":"‹name›, you are a dependable ‹race›. Can I count on you for another task?\nSome time ago I was surveying the cave to the north for minerals, and I left my favorite pick behind. When I later returned to retrieve it I found the cave was filled with vicious beasts! Will you go into the cave, the Burning Blade Coven, and get my pick?\nI left it in a chamber with waterfalls. My pick has a spell on it so you can see it in the dark, so you won't have to worry about finding it... just what's guarding it!","rew":"Money: 1 50 0 gold, 1 silver, 50 copper Experience: 450\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+150 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Have you entered the Burning Blade Coven, ‹name›? Did you find my pick?","done":"Great, you got it! Thanks a lot, ‹name›. This is my favorite pick! Now if my peons ever finish chopping down these trees, maybe we can find a nice cave to mine!","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":44.6,"y":68.7,"n":"Foreman Thazz'ril","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"794":{"id":794,"t":"Burning Blade Medallion","lv":5,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Burning Blade Medallion to Zureetha Fargaze, outside The Den.\nBurning Blade Medallion Yarrog Baneshadow","desc":"Through my divinations, I see that an item of power hides deep within the Burning Blade Coven, guarded by beasts and black magic.\nIt is called the Burning Blade Medallion, and your next task is to find it and remove it from the coven.\nBut be wary, for the medallion may be possessed by an agent of the Burning Blade, and if so then the agent's power would be greater than the familiars you have already encountered.\nGo, ‹name›. You will find the coven in a cave, to the north and west.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDust-covered Leggings Jagged Chain Vest Ripped Pants\nYou will also receive:\nMinor Healing Potion\nExperience: 675\n+200 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+200 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Is your task complete, ‹name›? Do you have the Burning Blade Medallion?","done":"You retrieved it! Well done!\nYour efforts within the Burning Blade Coven are key in rooting out this cult in the Valley of Trials. But I fear they have further aims in our land.\nWe have not seen the end of them.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":42.8,"y":69.1,"n":"Zureetha Fargaze","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"96874":{"id":96874,"t":"This is spinal axe","lv":10,"min":6,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Ug'thok in Orgrimmar wants you to collect 5 Weathered Spines from beasts in Thunder Ridge, along with 5 Rough Grinding Stones.\n5 Weathered Spine\n5 Rough Grinding Stone","desc":"Have you seen the huge beasts of Thunder Ridge? I keep thinking the spines on their backs would be perfect for crafting the head of a mighty axe. Saru laughed when I told him... but what does he know!?\nAs part of your smithing lessons, you can help me out! Bring me some of those spines, along with grinding stones to sharpen them.","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Rough Copper Chain Boots\nMoney: 2 50 0 gold, 2 silver, 50 copper Experience: 625\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Yes?","done":"These spines are tougher than I expected, Gehrfik! Crafting with them may not be as easy as I thought... but I'll keep working on it!\nOrgrimmar Durotar","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":80.6,"y":23.4,"n":"Ug'thok","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"154":{"id":154,"t":"Return the Comb","lv":24,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return the Ghost Hair Comb to Madame Eva in Darkshire.\nGhost Hair Comb\nProvided: Ghost Hair Comb","desc":"NO!!!!!\nTake it, take this comb away from me!\nI'm a monster, and no one will ever think me lovely again!","rew":"Money: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 200","back":"I sense that you have seen Blind Mary. You have my Comb...?","done":"I can make a spool of Ghost Hair Thread with this, and have a few strands to spare. Here are some coins for those extra strands.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":82,"y":59.1,"n":"Blind Mary","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":75.8,"y":45.3,"n":"Madame Eva","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"74":{"id":74,"t":"The Legend of Stalvan","lv":28,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"The Torn Journal page you discovered provides your next clue.\nA Torn Journal Page\nProvided: A Torn Journal Page","desc":"Inside the crate you find various objects: musty heirlooms, a family portrait, a few hunting trophies and some old books. Near the bottom, underneath a ceramic vase, you uncover A Torn Journal Page.","rew":"Experience: 1,150\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"What have you got there? I cannot see. My eyesight is very bad. Put it in my hands.","done":"I can barely make out those letters. But that writing style reminds me of something I once saw before my vision became so poor.\nStormwind City Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":42.5,"y":72,"n":"Sealed Crate","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":84.6,"y":69.4,"n":"Marshal Haggard","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"9194":{"id":9194,"t":"Craftsman's Writ - Runecloth Robe","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver 8 Runecloth Robes and the Craftsman's Writ - Runecloth Robe - to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nCraftsman's Writ - Runecloth Robe\n8 Runecloth Robe\nProvided: Craftsman's Writ - Runecloth Robe","desc":"The bearer of this writ is entitled to payment in the form of an insignia of their choice upon completion of the contracted work order.\nWork Order TR-7229:\n8 Runecloth Robes.\nAll filled orders should be delivered to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nContract is null and void if tampered with or damaged.\n-Dispatch Commander Metz, The Argent Dawn","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nInsignia of the Crusade Insignia of the Dawn\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Filling a work order, ‹class›?","done":"You shouldn't have! No really, you shouldn't have. I don't know what Metz is thinking, but nobody is going to be wearing these robes into Naxxramas.\n<Packmaster Stonebruiser sighs.>\nBah, another pile of junk I'll have to get transferred to the front lines and another berating I'll have to take from Chambers.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":70.7,"y":48.5,"n":"Packmaster Stonebruiser","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"1514":{"id":1514,"t":"Corrupted Windblossom","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"2 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a windblossom plant. The berries that hang from the plant appear rotten and poisonous. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply two Cenarion plant salves to the windblossom. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":55.2,"y":23.5,"n":"Corrupted Windblossom","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"6074":{"id":6074,"t":"The Hunter's Path","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Grif Wildheart in Kharanos.","desc":"Hello, young hunter. You look to me like you are skilled enough to handle a beast and train it as your companion.\nYou must see Grif Wildheart in Kharanos. He can put you on the path to earning a pet of your own.","rew":"Experience: 85","done":"Yes, I do believe you are ready, as well....","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":29.2,"y":67.5,"n":"Thorgas Grimson","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":45.8,"y":53,"n":"Grif Wildheart","e":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"8954":{"id":8954,"t":"Anthion's Parting Words","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Deliana in Ironforge with a set of Lightforge Boots, Lightforge Legplates and Lightforge Spaulders.\nLightforge Boots Balnazzar 0 %\nLightforge Legplates Baron Rivendare 0 % in Stratholme\nLightforge Spaulders The Beast 0 %\nProvided: Top Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet","desc":"Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet. In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.\nThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the medallion back together. Return to Deliana and tell her that Bodley is her only hope for finding the remaining pieces. Speak to her about any rewards you've arranged for.\nI, for once, shall rest in peace. I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!","rew":"You will receive:\nSoulforge Boots Soulforge Legplates Soulforge Spaulders\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You're back, ‹name›. You must tell me all about what you've found out. But first let us arrange for your reward.","done":"I can't believe our lives are all but forfeit all because of a stupid medallion! And you're sure Anthion mentioned Bodley?\nWell, you've done your job so let's get your reward out of the way.\nEastern Plaguelands Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":26.1,"y":11.3,"n":"Anthion Harmon","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8714":{"id":8714,"t":"Moonstrike the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"The heavens, in their countless stars, hold answers to earthly mysteries, ‹name›. Might, then, the wise, and the lucky, gaze up and find truth?","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":69.2,"y":73.4,"n":"Elder Moonstrike","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"8874":{"id":8874,"t":"The Lunar Festival","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Talk to the Lunar Festival Harbinger in the entrance to the Undercity. You can also talk to Lunar Festival Harbingers in other capital cities.","desc":"It's that time of the year, ‹name›! The Cenarion Circle invites all denizens of Azeroth to partake in our celebration of the Lunar Festival. You will find the Lunar Festival Harbinger in this very city at a location marked by a blessed circle of moonlight. She can tell you more about the holiday.","done":"Welcome, ‹name›. Are you here to join in the festivities?\nOrgrimmar Thunder Bluff Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":40.8,"y":30.5,"n":"Lunar Festival Herald","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":41.7,"y":32,"n":"Lunar Festival Harbinger","e":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":38.4,"y":63.4,"n":"Lunar Festival Herald","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":71.1,"y":28.2,"n":"Lunar Festival Harbinger","e":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.7,"y":72.8,"n":"Lunar Festival Herald","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.7,"y":72.7,"n":"Lunar Festival Harbinger","e":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"3114":{"id":3114,"t":"Glyphic Memorandum","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Glyphic Memorandum and speak to Marryk Nurribit inside Anvilmar above Coldridge Valley.\nGlyphic Memorandum\nProvided: Glyphic Memorandum","desc":"While you were helping me out, this memorandum was given to me to pass on to you. Take some time to read it when you have a chance. I'm thinkin' it came from the mage trainer Marryk. Take a gander at it and go find him inside Anvilmar when you've a chance.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Yeah, what's that, gnome? Speak up, if you don't mind. I don't hear so good after a few ales.","done":"Oh, yeah! Arcane Arts... of course.\nHere's what you need to know, ‹name›: Don't get into too much trouble. Save some coin to buy me an ale... or any spells ya might want. And stay the heck away from Gnomeregan. Other than that, have a good day! I'll be here if you need me or want to train... or whatever.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":29.9,"y":71.2,"n":"Sten Stoutarm","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":28.7,"y":66.4,"n":"Marryk Nurribit","e":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"9034":{"id":9034,"t":"Dreadnaught Breastplate","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Korfax at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a Dreadnaught Breastplate if you bring him the following items: 1 Desecrated Breastplate, 25 Wartorn Plate Scraps, 4 Arcanite Bars and 2 Nexus Crystals.\nDesecrated Breastplate\n25 Wartorn Plate Scrap Infectious Ghoul 22.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 21.6 % in Naxxramas , Plagued Deathhound 21.3 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 20.8 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n4 Arcanite Bar\n2 Nexus Crystal","desc":"During your battles with the Scourge in Naxxramas, should you come across desecrated battlements and wartorn plate scraps, return them to me and I shall craft for you a piece of armor worn by heroes.","rew":"You will receive:\nDreadnaught Breastplate\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Dreadnaught Breastplate.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":72,"y":48.5,"n":"Korfax, Champion of the Light","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"9114":{"id":9114,"t":"Shoulderpads of Faith","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Father Inigo Montoy at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Shoulderpads of Faith if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Shoulderpads, 12 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 2 Mooncloth and 3 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Shoulderpads Grobbulus 0 % in Naxxramas , Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Patchwerk 0 % in Naxxramas\n12 Wartorn Cloth Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 35 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 30.3 % in Naxxramas , Bile Retcher 28.5 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 28.3 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n2 Mooncloth\n3 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"<Father Montoy makes some strange gestures in the air in front of you.>\nBlessed boy/girl, have you found the vestments of the fallen? The poor souls whose last breaths were taken on the field of battle - stripped of everything including their dignity.\nBring me the desecrated remnants of the departed along with reagents of purification and you shall know faith.","rew":"You will receive:\nShoulderpads of Faith\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Have you brought me the reagents, child?","done":"The vestments are ready, ‹name›. Smite those that would harm our world in your righteous fire.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.6,"n":"Father Inigo Montoy","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"1434":{"id":1434,"t":"Befouled by Satyr","lv":33,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay 7 Hatefury Rogues, 7 Hatefury Felsworn, 7 Hatefury Betrayers, and 7 Hatefury Hellcallers, and return to Takata Steelblade in Desolace.\nHatefury Rogue slain : 0/ 7\nHatefury Felsworn slain : 0/ 7\nHatefury Betrayer slain : 0/ 7\nHatefury Hellcaller slain : 0/ 7","desc":"A demon infestation does not occur without other influences--something else allows evil to gain a foothold.\nIt may start with a weakened spirit, a needless desire for power; perhaps it's a thirst for revenge, or the appeal for final justice. When we are beset by pain, evil takes advantage of us--evil such as the satyr.\nTies have been made between them and the Burning Blade, and Thrall would have them slain. Seek them out to the northeast of here, and return to me when you've driven them back.","rew":"Experience: 2,650\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"I was warned by a tauren companion that the satyr are not all they appear to be. He believes there is something more to them, that their evil is a twisting of their true nature. But I have not seen such things.\nI see only the ruthless slaughter of the weak and the corruption of those who seek dark power.\nI will continue in my duty of annihilating them until the Warchief directs me otherwise. Until then, I take no pity on them.","done":"You have done well, ‹class›. You have shown honor and dedication.\nWhen our campaign in Desolace is done, the Warchief will know that you aided us in our actions here, and that you helped make his will manifest.\nI thank you.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":52.6,"y":54.4,"n":"Takata Steelblade","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"7834":{"id":7834,"t":"A Donation of Silk","lv":60,"min":26,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Silk Cloth Protector Weaver , Mountaineer Langarr 85.7 % , Watcher Wollpert 85.7 % , Mountaineer Zwarn 78.3 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 1,650\n+150 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"As with most other fabrics, our stocks of silk are at an all-time low. Our stores are such that we'd only need sixty pieces of silk from you total; we should be able to reach our goal with the support of others.\nA benevolent gift such as silk, might I add, would certainly increase your local standing in the community! If you have the sixty pieces of silk cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.","done":"Wonderful! We thank you for your generous donation, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":37.7,"y":87.9,"n":"Vehena","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"95034":{"id":95034,"t":"The debt","lv":24,"min":18,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Lumina Windsinger in the Sepulcher.\nSpeak with Lumina Windsinger","desc":"I think you should know that it wasn't actually the Gnolls who attacked us on the road.\nWe were actually attacked by a giant, wolf-like creature that I now know as a \"worgen\". It dispatched our guards and came for me, but Banon threw himself in its path. I managed to get a spell off which startled the creature, causing it to flee, but Banon was already badly bitten. He insisted I leave him there but I refused.\nWe were limping back here when the gnolls found us. What came next was terrifying...","done":"So now you understand. At the very end of his strength after being pierced by a dozen gnoll blades, he reared up to strike me. In that final moment we locked eyes, and I could tell he still knew who he was and that he recognized me. He knew what was happening but he had no control over himself. That was the worst part.\nIf such a thing is possible, I will see the creature that doomed him dead so that it can never visit this horror on another living thing. I swear it upon the sky above.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":43.2,"y":40.8,"n":"Lumina Windsinger","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5674":{"id":5674,"t":"Elune's Grace","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Priestess Alathea in Darnassus.","desc":"A wonderful day has come, ‹name›. You've reached the age in which our priests/priestesses are trained in abilities only Night elves know. But it is not for me to train you. You must return to the Temple of the Moon and speak to Priestess Alathea as soon as your business here is concluded. She will test you to ensure you're prepared, and only then will she teach you Elune's Grace.","rew":"You will learn: Elune's Grace\nExperience: 390","done":"By devoting yourself to Elune and our people, you have attained a state that not all of us can achieve. It is tradition that you then be taught even greater abilities for your devotion. Do you accept?","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":38.3,"y":81,"n":"Astarii Starseeker","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":39.5,"y":81.2,"n":"Priestess Alathea","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"8234":{"id":8234,"t":"Sealed Azure Bag","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve the Sealed Azure Bag from the Timbermaw Shaman in Azshara. Then take the bag to Archmage Xylem, also found in Azshara.\nSealed Azure Bag Timbermaw Shaman 0.4 %","desc":"First things first. What I've lost is a small blue bag, the contents of which are a private matter.\nDon't bother going after the thieves, because they are already dead. What we do know is the fools couldn't get the bag open. so they sold it to some timbermaw shaman in Azshara as a holy relic. Clever.\nI need you to travel to Azshara and retrieve it from the shaman through subtlety... or force. Better luck with the first method, I'd wager. Once acquired, take it to Archmage Xylem.","rew":"Money: 60 0 gold, 60 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,100\n+100 reputation with Ravenholdt","back":"Do I know you?","done":"I see you have Lord Ravenholdt's bag. Why didn't you say so, boy?\nAlterac Mountains Azshara","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":86,"y":78.9,"n":"Lord Jorach Ravenholdt","s":1},{"z":"Azshara","x":29.2,"y":40.2,"n":"Archmage Xylem","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"93034":{"id":93034,"t":"Valley of bones","lv":38,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Improve your reputation with the Gelkis, and locate Nerlokh near the Valley of Bones far east of Gelkis Village.\nGelkis Clan Centaur:\nLevel 38 , requires level 35 Difficulty 35 36 41 48 Side Both factions Quest ID 93034\nThe chain\n10 quests from level 32 to 38, 14,740 XP in all.\n1 [ 35 ] Strange Alliance\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Gelkis, then speak with Uthek the Wise.\nCaptain Pentigast Desolace\n2,050 XP\n2 [ 32 ] Raid on the Kolkar\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and bring 10 Crude Charms to Uthek the Wise in the Gelkis Village in Desolace.\nUthek the Wise Desolace\n2,550 XP\n[ 33 ] Gelkis Alliance\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Gelkis, then speak with Uthek the Wise.\nGurda Wildmane Desolace\n650 XP\n3 [ 35 ] Stealing Supplies\nBring 6 bags of Crudely Dried Meat to Uthek the Wise in the Gelkis Village.\nUthek the Wise Desolace\n1,350 XP\n4 [ 37 ] Ongeku\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and bring a Draenethyst Shard to Uthek the Wise in the Gelkis Village in Desolace.\nUthek the Wise Desolace\n2,850 XP\n5 [ 38 ] Valley of Bones this quest\nImprove your reputation with the Gelkis, and locate Nerlokh near the Valley of Bones far east of Gelkis Village.\n290 XP\n6 [ 38 ] Ravaging Ravagers\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis Clan and slay 6 Undead Ravagers, then return to Nerlokh at the southern entrance to Valley of Bones.\n1,450 XP\n7 [ 38 ] Facing the Truth\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis Clan, and bring an Accursed Skull and Gelkis Necromantic Garb to Uthek the Wise in Gelkis Village.\n700 XP\n8 [ 38 ] A Cleansing Cry\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and bring Tears of Theradras back to Uthek the Wise in Gelkis Village.\n2,150 XP\n9 [ 38 ] Test Your Theory\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and dispel the necromantic curse present on the Accursed Skull.\n700 XP","cats":["shendralas"]},"8314":{"id":8314,"t":"Unraveling the Mystery","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 4,950 experience instead of 5,300, 0.93 times as much.","obj":"Rutgar Glyphshaper at Bronzebeard's Encampment wants you to deliver the Glyphed Crystal Prism to Geologist Larksbane at the Cenarion Hold in Silithus.\nGlyphed Crystal Prism\nProvided: Glyphed Crystal Prism","desc":"We're on the verge of a breakthrough, ‹name›! The rubbings you recovered have allowed us to recreate the glyphs on this crystalline prism. They are apparently a means for the Qiraji and other unknown entities to communicate various messages to the silithid.\nUnfortunately, that is all we could get out of the glyphs. We need to find a way to unlock the messages hidden within the crystals.\nTake the glyphed crystal prism to Geologist Larksbane at Cenarion Hold. She might be able to help.","rew":"Experience: 4,950\n+75 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Oh my! What do you have there, ‹name›?","done":"The reason the dwarves could not decipher the glyphs is because there is nothing to decipher. The shifting outer layer of the prism must properly align with the inner crystal's markings in order for the message to be transmitted. Clever...\nWhile we should be able to translate this data, we must first unlock the code. There is only one clue on the surface of the prism - assuming the rubbings were transferred correctly - and it looks grim.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":41.3,"y":88.5,"n":"Rutgar Glyphshaper","s":1},{"z":"Silithus","x":49.7,"y":37.5,"n":"Geologist Larksbane","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"97914":{"id":97914,"t":"Expanding horizons","lv":17,"min":13,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring Thundris' Letter to Baros Alexston in Stormwind.\nThundris mentioned a boat in Auberdine that can take you there.\nProvided: Thundris' Letter","desc":"Auberdine is a humble place, ‹class›. You will not hear its name spoken in the boughs of Darnassus. Most reference only what the Sundering took from us--the thriving cities of Ameth'Aran, Bashal'Aran, and... Lathar'Lazal.\nYet Auberdine remains in their shadow.\nI would see our work here recognized. A new vessel connects us to the kingdom of Stormwind, bringing life and supplies to our shores. I beseech you join its next voyage, and bring this letter to a human called Baros Alexston.\nMake our home known.","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 0 silver, 90 copper Experience: 130","back":"I can smell the sea on you, friend!\n<Baros laughs.>\nWhat brings you to Stormwind?","done":"<Baros opens the letter and begins to read it, his smile fading.>\nDarkshore Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":37.4,"y":40.2,"n":"Thundris Windweaver","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49,"y":30.2,"n":"Baros Alexston","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"1274":{"id":1274,"t":"The Missing Diplomat","lv":28,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Bishop DeLavey in Stormwind Keep.","desc":"Excuse me, sir/madam. Bishop DeLavey asked me to approach adventurers that might be able to help him with a delicate matter.\nIf you could quietly head to Stormwind Keep and speak to him at your earliest convenience, I'm sure he would appreciate your help. Again, please be discreet. It is a matter of some importance.","rew":"Experience: 230","done":"Hello, ‹name›. I am Bishop DeLavey.\nNo doubt if you're asking me about my business here in the keep then young Thomas has succeeded in requisitioning you to help our kingdom. He has always been adept at following my requests.\nI'm afraid I don't have time to elaborate much, so allow me to be blunt... and please, try to keep this from becoming common knowledge.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.6,"y":44.5,"n":"Thomas","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":80.2,"y":44.1,"n":"Bishop DeLavey","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"394":{"id":394,"t":"The Head of the Beast","lv":31,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Mathias Shaw in Stormwind.","desc":"Find Shaw in Old Town. Let him know that the Lescovar threat has been dealt with and about your involvement in the Lord's plots against the city. I'm sure he'll be proud to have another hero among Stormwind's citizens.\nHe'll more than likely send you off to meet with the Prince or some other noble. Don't let it get to your head, ‹name›. The nobles can think they rule the city all they want, but some things remain out of their hands.","rew":"Experience: 250","done":"He is dead, then? Your justice was swift, ‹name›. I pray to the Light that I never become your quarry!\n<He laughs and claps you on the shoulder.>\nI mean no criticism, ‹name›. How could I, being the master of all assassins? But in truth, you have done the people of Stormwind a great service, and for that, I thank you.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":66,"y":74.1,"n":"Elling Trias","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":78.3,"y":70.7,"n":"Master Mathias Shaw","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"8554":{"id":8554,"t":"Facing Negolash","lv":50,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 35 instead of 40.","obj":"Bring 10 Barbecued Buzzard Wings and 5 bottles of Junglevine Wine to Captain Smotts' Lifeboat.\nKill Negolash, and bring Smotts' Cutlass to Captain Smotts in Stranglethorn.\nSmotts' Cutlass Negolash","desc":"Negolash is a hungry giant.\nWhen the giants destroyed our ship, Negolash went straight for my kitchen. He wasn't hungry for crew like the other giants. Negolash wanted wine...and my Barbecued Buzzard Wings. They're my specialty, and I had to go all the way to the Badlands for the recipe!\nIf you want to lure the giant, then get some wine and a heap of buzzard wings. Put them in our old lifeboat, southeast of here along the coast. When Negolash smells all that food, he'll come for sure!","rew":"You will receive:\nSmotts' Compass\nExperience: 7,100\n+200 reputation with Booty Bay\n-1,000 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Did you get my cutlass, ‹name›?","done":"You got my cutlass from Negolash! I can't believe my fortune, ‹name›! Meeting you has turned my luck to the better, make no mistake there!\nThank you! And if I ever get a new ship and you're looking to sail the seas, you would be my honored guest.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":26.7,"y":73.6,"n":"Sprogger","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":26.7,"y":73.6,"n":"Captain Hecklebury Smotts","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8074":{"id":8074,"t":"Paragons of Power: The Augur's Belt","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 6,500, 1.02 times as much.","obj":"Bring Maywiki of Zuldazar a Primal Hakkari Girdle. You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Honored with the Zandalar Tribe.\nMaywiki of Zuldazar is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\nPrimal Hakkari Girdle\nReach 9000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","desc":"Augurs know the mojo of the elements, mon. They use it as a means to guide the tribe to glory. In the dark days after the Gurubashi Empire ripped itself up, our augurs led us to our safe haven in the South Seas. They've also led us back here to the Vale, right back to the heart of evil brewin' in Zul'Gurub.\nBring me an offerin' of the Paragons of Power from inside Zul'Gurub and prove your worth to us. Do it and I'll give ya a belt that our augurs use - one with powerful mojo inside it!","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Augur's Belt\nExperience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"The Paragons of Power are what I need mon - we'll tap the power right out of them in our fight against the evil from Zul'Gurub. Do ya have them for me?","done":"I can smell the scent of vanquished evil on ya, ‹name›. It's a sweet smell mon... one I think you know quite well.\nI know it's no small feat to have brought me the Paragons of Power required for the belt. Your deeds have not only honored the tribe, but also honored yourself amongst my tribe. Here ya are - take the augur's belt and don it as your own!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16,"n":"Maywiki of Zuldazar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"2874":{"id":2874,"t":"Deliver to MacKinley","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Stoley's Bottle to \"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley in Booty Bay.\nStoley's Bottle\nProvided: Stoley's Bottle","desc":"Thanks again for your help, ‹name›. Here's a bottle of Steamwheedle bilge rum. Take it to MacKinley and he can finally put to rest his crazy beliefs about Booty Bay booze.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSwashbuckler Sash Shinkicker Boots\nMoney: 50 0 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,900","back":"Did Stoley cough up my booze?","done":"Hm, let's try this...\nI can't believe it! This stuff is... terrible! That's great!\nWell I guess Stoley can keep the money he owes me. He's true to his word about Steamwheedle bilge rum. That stuff is as thick as gravel and burns like lava!\nTanaris Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":67.1,"y":24,"n":"Stoley","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.8,"y":77.1,"n":"\"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"2954":{"id":2954,"t":"The Stone Watcher","lv":50,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Learn the purpose of the Stone Watcher of Norgannon, and then interact with the Uldum Pedestal in the Tanaris desert.","desc":"\"Salutations - I am a guardian of entry. Unless you have the Plates of Uldum already integrated with your disc set, I will not allow for entry into the Uldum compound.\"\nThe appearance of the Stone Watcher of Norgannon must be the reaction that was hoped for in sending you out to the Tanaris desert with the platinum discs. As instructed, you will need to find out what the story behind the Stone Watcher is before continuing on.","rew":"Experience: 4,700","back":"The purpose of the stone watcher must be learned before continuing on...","done":"The stone watcher's voice resonates with power and authority:\n\"Your discs will be returned to you once you access the pedestal. When you have obtained the Plates of Uldum and incorporated them into your existing disc set, you may then enter the complex.\"","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":37.6,"y":81.4,"n":"Uldum Pedestal","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"874":{"id":874,"t":"Mahren Skyseer","lv":27,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Mahren Skyseer.","desc":"You have hunted the beasts of the Barrens. Your spirit is strong. But a hunter must always be prepared. A true hunter can stalk prey down any path. Mountains and swamps will not sway him/her.\nNot even the sea.\nFind my sister, Mahren. She hunts the great water beasts along the coast. She will be your teacher in their ways.\nBut be wary in your search for her, for the Barrens' coast is held by humans.","rew":"Experience: 550\n+25 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"My brother sent you, did he? Then you must have proven yourself to him. If you have earned the respect of Jorn, then you have my respect as well.\nAre you ready to tread farther down the hunter's path?","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":44.9,"y":59.1,"n":"Jorn Skyseer","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":65.8,"y":43.9,"n":"Mahren Skyseer","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"3514":{"id":3514,"t":"Horde Presence","lv":29,"min":15,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Runed Gauntlets. Read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Kill the leader of the Talon Den, Rynthariel the Keymaster.\nRynthariel the Keymaster slain\nProvided: Kadrak's Flag","desc":"This scroll is from that scheming dryad Rynthariel, Keymaster of the Talon Den on Stonetalon Peak.\nShe'll not be making any more contact with the messenger you looted this from, heh, but we must stand our ground here. The Horde will not tolerate her outrunners here.\n‹name›, travel to the Talon Den. Kill Rynthariel, and then put up a symbol for all to see. Take this Horde flag, ‹name›. Put it up in the Talon Den so that they will not be so rash as to send another messenger through our territory again.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nTrailblazer Boots Jutebraid Gloves Runed Gauntlets\nNew in Forever: Runed Gauntlets.\nExperience: 2,950\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"We cannot allow the Alliance on our land, ‹name›. Make this known.","done":"You're a tough one! Ridding the Den of Rynthariel is a major step, ‹name›. They will be slow to regroup, and so we can count on less Alliance runners in the Barrens. They will think again before sending another this way.\nThank you.\nThe Barrens Stonetalon Mountains","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":48.1,"y":5.4,"n":"Kadrak","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"96394":{"id":96394,"t":"The Restless Dead","lv":15,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Kill 15 Enraged Apparitions, 10 Tormented Souls and put the spirit of Anvilmar to rest.\nEnraged Apparition slain : 0/ 15\nTormented Soul slain : 0/ 10","desc":"Something has disturbed the tombs down in the Hall of Thanes, and strange noises have been heard coming from deep within the vaults. The spirits of the dead are light sleepers, and whatever is going on down there seems to have startled them.\nHead down there and see what you can do about that for us. If any of the dead are awake--well, put them back down!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDusty Belt Cryptwalker Bracers\nMoney: 7 0 gold, 7 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,300\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","done":"Ah good, its done then. I can't have the other keepers refusing to enter the hall to do their duties on account of \"ghosts\" and \"angry dead\", can I?","pins":[{"z":"Ironforge","x":33,"y":48,"n":"Afadra Dunwall","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-hall-of-thanes"]},"1114":{"id":1114,"t":"Delivery to the Gnomes","lv":36,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Delicate Car Parts to Fizzle Brassbolts in Shimmering Flats.\nDelicate Car Parts\nProvided: Delicate Car Parts","desc":"Now that I have what I need, give these parts to Fizzle Brassbolts. He's been waiting a long time for them -- I'm sure he won't miss the little piece I removed from his order...\nAnd I wouldn't bother mentioning it to him. It was small and worthless.\nTrust me.","rew":"Money: 10 0 gold, 10 silver, 0 copper Experience: 700","back":"You have something for me? That's great! let's see it!","done":"There they are! My hydro ratchets and repeater bolts! These will do just fine. Thank you!","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":77.8,"y":77.3,"n":"Kravel Koalbeard","s":1},{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":78.1,"y":77.1,"n":"Fizzle Brassbolts","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"1194":{"id":1194,"t":"Rizzle's Schematics","lv":41,"min":29,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Sample of Indurium Ore to Pozzik on the Shimmering Flats.\nProvided: Sample of Indurium Ore","desc":"Rizzle's schematics describe the process of the refinement of indurium ore. From his scrawls, it is apparent that indurium ore is being obtained from the dwarven excavation site of Uldaman in the Badlands.\nMuch of the other notes relate to the heat resistant properties.\nUsed as a paperweight for the plans is a hunk of what appears to be unrefined indurium ore.","rew":"Experience: 1,650\n+50 reputation with Ratchet","done":"Indurium? Interesting... If it is capable of resisting heat to the degree that you say, it would explain the performance increase the gnomes have displayed of late.\nThis sample you've brought to me will be invaluable, also. I will be able to perform some tests on this, but I'll need more for this to actually be of any use to us.","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":77.2,"y":77.4,"n":"Rizzle's Unguarded Plans","s":1},{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":80.2,"y":75.9,"n":"Pozzik","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"3914":{"id":3914,"t":"Linken's Sword","lv":52,"min":47,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver Linken's Superior Sword to Linken in Un'Goro Crater.\nLinken's Superior Sword\nProvided: Linken's Superior Sword","desc":"After a strong flash of light, you are able to pick up the sword again. It has been transformed!","rew":"Money: 75 0 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,100","back":"Oh! I remember you! You are... No, don't tell me!","done":"My sword... It's finished!\nNow, if only I could remember why I needed this...\nHere, let me at least pay you for your work.\nTanaris Un'Goro Crater","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":53.8,"y":29.1,"n":"A Conspicuous Gravestone","s":1},{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":44.7,"y":8.1,"n":"Linken","e":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"5514":{"id":5514,"t":"Mold Rhymes With...","lv":57,"min":55,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -15g instead of 0.","obj":"Bring the Imbued Skeletal Fragments and 15 gold coins to Krinkle Goodsteel in Gadgetzan.\nImbued Skeletal Fragments\nProvided: Imbued Skeletal Fragments","desc":"The goblin you will need to speak with is Krinkle Goodsteel. He peddles his skills to the highest bidder in Gadgetzan, within the Tanaris desert. He'll likely be the only one who can produce the mold we need, and his services won't come cheap. We now ask for you to dig deep by footing whatever fee he will charge.\nI'm an apothecary, not a banker. If I had gold lying around, I certainly wouldn't be here.\nI guess I said the quiet part out loud again. Oops.\nGadgetzan awaits you! Good luck!","rew":"Experience: 600","back":"Yeah, I know who you are, and I know why you're here. Dithers sent word to me before you arrived. Let's cut to deal at hand, now shall we?\nI've got a mold you can use for the skeleton key, but it will cost you - fifteen gold, up front, no negotiation. I'll pack the skeletal fragments into the mold for you, and I'll also teach you on how to forge the stem of the key without any knowledge of blacksmithing... all free of charge no less.\nWho says mercenaries don't offer competitive deals!","done":"Dithers said you'd deliver the goods, and deliver you have! A deal is a deal; let me pack the fragments into the mold for you.\nDid Dithers imbue them already? Excellent... otherwise, it would have been a long trip back to the Bulwark for you.\nTirisfal Glades Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83.3,"y":69.2,"n":"Apothecary Dithers","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.5,"y":28.8,"n":"Krinkle Goodsteel","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"634":{"id":634,"t":"Plea To The Alliance","lv":31,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Seek out Captain Nials at Refuge Pointe.","desc":"I ask of you one more small favor, ‹class›. We await the reserves of Ironforge. However, Roggo has knowledge of an Alliance camp to the north in Arathi Highlands at Refuge Pointe.\nTravel there and seek out Captain Nials. Ask the good Captain if the Alliance can spare some soldiers to help us reclaim Dun Modr and the Thandol Span.","rew":"Experience: 1,250","done":"My condolences go out to Longbraid and his brave soldiers. The news of the Thandol Span tragedy and the fall of Dun Modr hangs heavy in my heart.\nBut Stromgarde has fallen! Hence our presence here at Refuge Pointe. We are faced with retaking our own great city.\nHonor and duty require that we do not leave the Highlands until Stromgarde raises the mighty banner of the King once again. I will send word to Longbraid that he is on his own...\nWetlands Arathi Highlands","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":49.9,"y":18.2,"n":"Rhag Garmason","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":45.8,"y":47.6,"n":"Captain Nials","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"474":{"id":474,"t":"Defeat Nek'rosh","lv":32,"min":23,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Chieftain Nek'rosh\nBring Nek'rosh's Head to Captain Stoutfist.\nNek'rosh's Head Chieftain Nek'rosh","desc":"Now that the catapults have been burned, find and kill Chieftain Nek'rosh.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nAncient War Sword Barreling Reaper\nExperience: 2,550\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Have you killed Nek'rosh?","done":"Stoutly done, ‹name›. You have dealt a telling blow to the Dragonmaw orc clan. They may never recover. And the destruction of those catapults has made Menethil Harbor safe.\nYou are a ‹race› of merit, and the kingdom of Ironforge rewards those who serve it well.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":47.5,"y":47,"n":"Dragonmaw Catapult","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":9.9,"y":57.5,"n":"Captain Stoutfist","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"92474":{"id":92474,"t":"Falling with style","lv":2,"min":2,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Jump from the top of the watchtower in Thendal Grove and use your Walk on Air ability to slow your fall.","desc":"Well hello there, ‹name›! Want to play a game?\nAll you've got to do is step up on that ledge... then jump! Use your innate ability to walk on the air to slow your fall and see how far forward you can float.\nThe rules are made up and the points don't matter, but you get bonus points if you can land right in front of Rorian the Dayseeker and startle him! He won't like it but I'll certainly get a good laugh if you can get him all worked up! Hah!","back":"Using your ability to walk on air can get you out of--and, well... into--all kinds of trouble!","done":"How many times do I need to tell Myriaal not to encourage others to make reckless usage of our skyborne gifts!\nThat being said, I suppose that a little bit of practice in the relative safety of the village is... acceptable.\nIn the future I'd simply suggest you to use your ability judiciously. You do not want to exhaust your magic thoughtlessly and then not be able to use it when you truly need it.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":43.6,"y":24,"n":"Myriaal Mistwake","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":42,"y":23.4,"n":"Rorian the Dayseeker","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]}});